Suppress every non-guest overlay MAME draws into the video pipeline.

WHY. A Kernel Hive station streams ONE thing: the machine's own framebuffer.
MAME's UI layer composes its own primitives onto the same target — the
savestate popmessage ("Loaded state from <path>. Warning: Save states are not
officially supported for this system." — seen by the operator on a golden
restore, 2026-08-12), the FPS/profiler overlays, the menu system, the paused
banner. None of that is the exhibit; a visitor seeing emulator chrome on a
1982 Dragon 32 screen is looking at the wrong machine.

`-skip_gameinfo` and `skip_warnings 1` each remove ONE such screen and neither
touches popmessage, so the fix belongs at the seam where UI primitives enter a
render target rather than at the dozen sites that raise them. render_target
composes the UI container into every target's primitive list; gating that one
condition removes all of it at once, for every renderer (drawshm included) and
every target, with no per-message allow-list to keep in sync with upstream.

GATED AT RUNTIME, like every other patch in this stack: with MAME_NO_UI unset
the tree behaves exactly as upstream, so the same binary still shows its UI if
anyone ever runs it by hand to debug a machine. The stations set it in
streamhost/stations/mame-native/x11-runtime.sh.

NOT the same thing as input: the UI's INPUT path (menus reachable by Tab) is
untouched — these stations simply never deliver those keys, and a keymap only
carries fields the machine itself declares.

diff --git a/src/emu/render.cpp b/src/emu/render.cpp
--- a/src/emu/render.cpp
